An email communication sent by an insurance broker, placing broker, or reinsurance
broker to an underwriter, insurer, or market participant, presenting a new or renewal
insurance or reinsurance risk for consideration, requesting terms, capacity, or
support, or providing placement-related information and updates in connection with
an insurance transaction.
These documents usually:
- Are formatted as email messages, identifiable by salutation (e.g. "Hi", "Dear"),
  a conversational or semi-formal tone, sender sign-off with the broker's name,
  title, firm, contact details, and regulatory footer disclosures (e.g. FCA
  authorisation, registered company details, privacy notices)
- Are authored by a named broker or placing professional at a recognised insurance
  or reinsurance broking firm (e.g. Marsh, WTW, Lockton, Bowring Marsh, McGill
  Partners, Aon, or similar) acting on behalf of an insured or cedant
- Present a specific risk, account, or placement opportunity to the recipient
  underwriter or market, using language such as "we are looking for your support",
  "would this be of interest", "we are doing a remarket", "please see enclosed a
  new submission", "we are seeking capacity", or "can you provide terms"
- Describe the insured's business operations, industry sector, geographic footprint,
  revenue, and other relevant underwriting information in narrative or bullet-point
  format embedded within the email body
- May include key underwriting data such as limits requested, program structure
  (primary, excess, tower layers), premium indications or targets, deductibles,
  sublimits, coverage lines sought (e.g. General Liability, Excess Liability,
  Property, Auto, Umbrella, Political Risk, D&O), commission, and wording references
- May summarise loss history or claims experience (e.g. total paid, total incurred,
  largest single loss) in the email body as part of the risk presentation
- May reference or list attached documents (e.g. submission pack, loss runs,
  exposure workbooks, coverage requests, slip, financials, renewal slides) without
  those attachments being part of the classified document itself
- May relate to any class of insurance business including but not limited to:
  Casualty/Liability (General Liability, Excess Liability, Umbrella, Auto),
  Property (facultative reinsurance, all-risks, CAT), Political Risk, Trade Credit,
  Directors & Officers, Professional Indemnity, or specialty lines
- May cover new business placements, renewals, remarketing exercises, requests
  for additional capacity, lineslip support, or facultative reinsurance placements
- May include internal forwarding notes, log entries, or brief covering messages
  from one broker to another within the same firm (e.g. "just for logging for now
  whilst we await more information") that form part of the email chain related to
  a placement

